{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be","id":185837,"title":"What Kindred Would You Be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-01T16:41:45-07:00","id":185837,"title":"What Kindred Would You Be?","content":"So I made a post on Changeling asking what kind of Kiths everyone would be, but now I'm curious as to what kind of vampire you would be if the World of Darkness were a real thing.<br /> <br /> <b>What to List:</b><br /> <br /> Clan<br /> <br /> Covenant<br /> <br /> Reasons:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional Listing:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodline<br /> <br /> Disciplines<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> So here's me! ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons:</b> I make no attempt to hide the fact that the downgrading of vampires in the recent decades infuriates me. I am a horror genre fan, and I love it when vampires are portrayed as monsters as opposed to sex symbols. If I had the choice of clan, I would definitely pick Nosferatu, for they are the very personification of monsters. Gangrel would be a close runner up, however. I'd be one of the Nosferatu who embraces their nature and takes delight in flaunting it around the pretty folk. In some poetic way, I actually find the Nosferatu to be more beautiful than the bustiest of Daeva.<br /> <br /> As for the Covenant, as I mentioned on my Kiths topic, I like the idea of magic and sorcery, so a covenant who practices blood magic would certainly appeal to me. I'd just need to build up a pain tolerance, I suppose. A runner up choice would be the Carthian Movement, as I feel that the feudal era system of vampire society is ridiculous and needs to wake up to the fact that the class system is dead and gone. The Invictus and the Lancea Sanctum can go fuck themselves, and I don't like the goals of the Ordo Dracul (like I said, I like vampires being monstrous). Being Unaligned may sound like a good way to go, but in a society that thrives on betrayal, I'd rather have some kind of back up than face an army alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Malkavian Afflicted or the Noctuku<br /> <br /> Even as a human I'm not completely all there, and have had a string of mental conditions throughout my life. So what better way to join the undead than as a raving lunatic and &quot;spread the love&quot; with Dementation? Alternatively, if you're going to be a predator, why not be an apex predator? Sure, as a Noctuku I'd be terrifying to the rest of the community, but as I've already said that's exactly how I like my vampires to be. Besides, I don't think locating food would be as difficult as most people think. Vampires can regenerate, so just lock one up in your basement and you'd have a renewable food supply!<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Nightmare, Vigor, Resilience, Protean, Cruac, Dementation or Phagia (depending on bloodline), Animalism<br /> <br /> <br /> As a vampire, I would train in Vigor and Resilience for the sweet, sweet pleasure of beating the crap out of my enemies in close quarters. I would train in Nightmare to appear more terrifying and appeal to my interpretation of vampires. I would of course study Cruac as a member of the Circle, and I would put in the effort to learn the power of Protean for the added benefit of having a set of retractable claws in battle, or the awesomeness of being able to turn into a variety of different animals. Speaking of animals, I like them more than I like people. Especially cats, I'm a cat lover, I want a haven guarded by Ghouled house cats!<br /> <br /> As for the bloodline Disciplines, either I could drive people insane as a Malkavian afflicted, or I could tear their skin off and wear it like a suit as a Noctuku. Either one sounds enticing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-09-2014, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T17:13:44-07:00","id":185856,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Invictus<br /> <br /> I don't have the physicality of the Gangrel or the potent charismatic force needed for being a Daeva or Ventrue, and I just sincerely hope no one hates me enough to make me a Nosferatu. That just leaves the lovely, lonely Mekhet, all prone to watching and study and brooding. They're a pleasant fit for me, and the idea of having Auspex and Obfuscate to be the perfect fly on the wall would make me a happy little Leech indeed.<br /> <br /> As for the Covenants, I know my choice isn't the popular one, but hear me out. I've got no desire to ever climb the ladder and end up Prince, and am quite happy being a cog in the grand machine. The Masquerade is the best option for Kindred and kine alike. Maintaining order is important. Discipline is crucial to keeping the Kindred safe. Contrast with the other options; a fiery church that I have no faith in, a bunch of disorganized rabble that want to destroy the Masquerade, and some insane pagan throwbacks. I've got no beef with the Ordo - figuring out just what the hell I am is a fascinating goal, believe me - but I've not got the medical or occult chops for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:17:16-07:00","id":185942,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan: </b>Nosferatu<br /> <br /> I'm pretty much a social isolate as it is, mostly happy with that. I'm also not curious enough for a Mekhet, so their stealthy, antisocial cousins it is! ..That, and I hate violence, with Nightmare being a potent nonlethal tool. That, and I live in the center of a forest (&quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IUmkf_l38fA\" target=\"_blank\">There's a man in the woods!</a>&quot;).<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Lanecea et Sanctum<br /> <br /> I really, really wanted to put Ordo Dracul here, but really? Knowing me, I'd interpret being Embraced as a sign of something both spiritual and dangerous, and that smells of conversion bait - and I like my Humanity, thank you. I'm also a lover of hoarding knowledge, so they'd probably be happy to offer that as well. Probably be part of the go-between brigade, soothing ruptures between interpretations and other Covenants because I ain't that zealous. And of course, no inherent violence, just a blank check to indulge my righteous ire - anger issues when faced with dicks and the willfully ignorant is a common reaction with me. Plus, Theban Sorcery. Gotta love that.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline: </b>Moroi<br /> <br /> Yeah, Dragons, but I'd imagine they'd be all too happy to provide an Avus in return for serving as ambassador/errand boy. That Animalism Discipline just works for a Haunt in the middle of the woods, possibly a killer (not actually, but possibly). Especially with the nerfed weakness, I'm more of a scholar than anything, and now that is very possible for Gangrel in general, let alone pseudo-Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-01-2014, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T21:26:08-07:00","id":185989,"title":"","content":"Ooh! I love these kinds of things!<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Mekhet<br /> <br /> As an INTP, Mekhet seems like a nearly perfect fit for me. My greatest skill has always been my ability to intuitively understand people's thoughts and emotions. Even as a young child, I just understood people's thoughts and feelings, which made me an excellent listener. As I grew older I studied psychology and developed an understanding of those processes from an intellectual level as well. In short, I have IRL Auspex. I almost went with Daeva, because I am also very charismatic. But ultimately I think Mekhet is still more appropriate because my social skills come not from raw magnetism, but subtle application of psychology and acting. My aforementioned knack for knowing what and how people think, coupled with my ability to outwardly display what ever emotions I want, allows me to manipulate social situations with ease, but in a way that more closely resembles clever use of Auspex and Obfuscate to garner bonuses on mundane social rolls than outright control via Majesty. Not to mention despite being very socially skilled, I'm actually extremely introverted, which doesn't mean too much on its own, but alongside all of these other points in favor of Mekhet over Daeva, it adds up. Additionally, I'm very intellectually driven. No desire is stronger for me than my curiosity and drive to explore and understand the mysterious and unknown, and I think that more than anything is what the Mekhet are all about.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> From the very first time I read Vampre: the Requeim, I knew this was the Covenant for me. Something about them struck a chord on a level I can't explain in words. Their goals, their ideology, their methodology, their reverence for the coolest vampire character ever written. Everything about them just resonates with me on a deep personal level. I find their goals to be the most noble out of all of the Covenants. The Invictus and the Carthians are just two sides of the same old political coin, and I honestly find both equally petty. The Sanctified scare the hell out of me, seriously, what the fuck. They combine all the worst parts of organized religion and twist them into something far more sinister and, honestly, dangerous. The Crone I could probably get along with fine; even if I don't agree with their religious views, they seem pretty content to let me believe what I want if I let them believe what they want, and I can respect that. But the Order really has the right idea - the pursuit of personal enlightenment and self-improvement, that takes a different form for each individual. What more respectable goal could anyone ask for than that? I could go on, but I'll leave it at that for now.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> None<br /> <br /> I freaking love the Morbus and would really love to be able to say I would be one, but if I'm being honest with myself, I would not join a bloodline. I wouldn't want to get myself involved with any group as insular as a bloodline, and would be much happier finding my own path. Maybe after I had followed my path along the Coils to a point where I felt I had made a breakthrough truly worth sharing I might start my own bloodline (if my blood was potent enough) and let my insight guide them down their own paths. But I would not join any existing line.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Majesty, Obfuscate, and as many Coils and Scales as I could learn (Voivode primary)<br /> <br /> Pretty much the reasons above explain my Discipline choices as well. I know Majesty is out-of-clan, but I'm sure I could find a Daeva to teach me at least a little of it. Also, I'd probably join the Moirai Shadow Cult if I could, and one of their benefits is in-clan Majesty for Mekhet members and in-clan Auspex for Daeva members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-02-2014, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T21:28:49-07:00","id":185993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be#post185837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pussification</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Sexist slurs are not acceptable.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T22:36:19-07:00","id":186048,"title":"","content":"Clan: Daeva<br /> <br /> Covenant: Ordo or Invictus<br /> <br /> Reasons: It might be sign that I have worked in the bar and entertainment industries for to long, but I have learned that people really are meat puppets. If you know when to give a complement, the proper way to establish physical contact, and how to hold your posture you can pretty much control the entire social interaction and they are just kind off dragged along for the ride. So I feel the Daeva would be a pretty good fit.<br /> <br /> As for Covenant, I am a transhumnist at heart so the Ordo really speak to me. I am also a realist which give the Invictus a certain appeal. I'm not a religious person at all, so that strikes out the to religion centered covenants. I can't help but view the Movement as nothing more than a mob of ineffectual rabble rousers at best, meaning I wouldn't feel at home with them ether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","user":"sciurrus","date":". 07-02-2014, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","name":"sciurrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T23:20:36-07:00","id":186062,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Mekhet<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> I really don't know. Carthian Movement? I might delve into the Ordo Dracul just because being a vampire is being extremely weak, and Coils can help me live better. Or maybe not. I find Covenants to be too inhuman for my taste.<br /> <b>Bloodlines:</b>Not really.<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, probably 1 dot in Majesty some time or the other.<br /> <i>Reasons</i>:I'm an introverted, empathic, emotional sponge guy. I think a lot and search a lot. I would probably look for someone to teach me the first dot of Majesty because I like when people care about me. I would also attempt to stay as human as possible, avoid killing, avoid frenzy, be extremely careful about my Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T00:49:06-07:00","id":186110,"title":"","content":"Clan: Ventrue <br /> <br /> covenant: Invictus <br /> <br /> I've always liked the Ventrue as far back as owod. Plus now they get off easy as hell with their clan bane. I always felt the Invictus is what a vampire society would be like if real so that appeals to me. <br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodline: Sons of Cade <br /> <br /> The description of Cade and his bloodline makes me imagine riding around the American southwest playing Blood Meridian for a few hundred years. <br /> <br /> <br /> Disciplines: Animialism, Dominate, Protean, Resilience, Culter Mithras. <br /> <br /> Ability to walk in the sun again sounds mighty nice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T07:21:09-07:00","id":186289,"title":"","content":"Clan Ventrue, Invictus<br /> <br /> In my mortal days I may be very far left of the centre, politics-wise but when I am literally a blood sucking parasite/predator I'm going all the way. Probably try to get myself some Vigour to boot, but what I'm going for is &quot;I got mine, jack.&quot; I'm siding with the winners and I <i>want my fucking mansion.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:02:45-07:00","id":187337,"title":"","content":"Clan: Gangrel<br /> <br /> Covenant: Carthian Movement.<br /> <br /> Reasons: My reasoning for Gangrel is rather simple: I love the idea of a ever shifting body and the the changes such a mutable form would bring each night, for either peaceful utility, hunting, or defending myself from kindred rivals. It doesn't hurt that I have a naturally rough and aggressive attitude to begin with, and the predatory and gruff nature of many Gangrel would fit quite well with me. For a much less vampiric reason, I would find the ability to become a number of different animals to be truly enlightening. Flying, swimming, leaping from tree branch to tree branch or digging beneath the ground- these are all perspectives that could truly help one think and inspect their own natures. Compounding that insight is the amount of understanding that Animalism provides- sure it may be primarily commanding the beasts around them, but it still provides clearer methods of communication between vampire and animal. As for Covenant, the New Blood and Smoke Carthians have a certain appeal to them that the older Carthian Movement worked too hard for. I for one like cooperation, not in a socialist sense like some people incorrectly peg the Movement as, but cooperation in a predatory way that just happens to appeal to human concepts of innovation and change.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Larvae<br /> <br /> The martial prowess and the supernatural speed of the Larvae bloodline would also serve me very well in my duties ( as I am currently studying Criminal Justice and plan to go into law enforcement), and I can live with the weakness they have- the ends justify the means in my opinion lol.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Animalism, Resilience, Protean, Celerity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:16:51-07:00","id":187346,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Ventrue<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons</b>: Would only be Ventrue simply for the Malkovian Bloodline. If I could, I would hands-down pick the old Malkavian however. I am a joker and a loner. I always felt that old Malkavians liked to hide in plain site. Social outcasts due to their mentality, but if you got to know them you would have a great time.<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul because it makes life easier. As a Malkavian, they have it rough enough as it is. (Plus that last time I played one, he was obsessed about being able to walk during the day. Completely power hungry but that's beside the point. He was making a suit similar to that in Repo: The Genetic Opera. Synthetic material, completely sealed, only way to see through the helmet was through a camera system. Had tiny cameras on all parts of his body and the inside of the helmet was all LCD displays.)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodlines:</b> Malkovian if unable to go old school Malkavian<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Vigor, Celerity, Resilience, Dementation (if possible), Obfuscate, and as many Coils and Scales as possible, starting with the Ascendant<br /> (If not Dementation, then Nightmares and Majesty to get the devotions that are similar to some Dementation abilities)<br /> <br /> Would rock all of the physical disciplines. Vigor to beat all of my opponents to a pulp. Resilience to help deal with the sunlight and Celerity to quickly run to shelter if need be. Dementation as I love the idea of using your madness to effect others (Passions.. That is all). Obfuscate to continue to hide in plain site.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:25:05-07:00","id":187361,"title":"","content":"Clan:Mekhet<br /> <br /> Covenant:Unaligned<br /> <br /> Bloodline:None<br /> <br /> Reasons:If I found myself as a Vampire I would react by becoming withdrawn and reclusive so as not to cause harm to my friends and loved ones,a monster I may be now but I still have my mind and emotions.I would no doubt have to leave my current life behind for the safety of others and take to being a wanderer,only stopping when I'm sure its safe and I can set up roots that isn't likely going to lead back to my old life.I will interact with regular humans as normal,but I will be cautionous as to avoid forming bonds,least I cause more pain.And speaking of pain I would only feed out of necessity,taking only what I need to survive.No more,no less.I would do my best to avoid other Vamps as best I can,partially out of a desire not to interact with them but also because of the fear of diablerie.No doubt I would get a good deal of use out of Auspex and Obfuscate in this new life I find myself in.<br /> <br /> None of the Covenants appeal to me on a personal level so I can't say I would join any of them.The Carthians are a maybe,but that would mean dealing with other Vampires.<br /> <br /> Disciplines:Auspex,Obfuscate,Celerity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/f6wpurj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/5hsbn8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/249-nitemare17","name":"Nitemare17","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T16:53:26-07:00","id":187512,"title":"","content":"Clan: Mekhet (irrelevant in part, see below)<br /> <br /> I won't be identifying myself as anything more than Sta-Au, the wicked and cruel ones, the twice-dead. It will colour things initially, but eventually I'll change and progress enough that identifying along those lines is pointless. The merit to feed off other supernaturals and remain nourished after a strong Blood Potency would be quick, either earlier (just waiting) because of the Bloodline, Ordo experimentation or something else. Besides, wandering as a ghost I'll be able to attack them for Essence anyhow.<br /> <br /> Never see me coming, and I already know everything about you before you even open your mouth to lie. Astute to patterns, the rotten core under the veneer and a precision predator. Can't hit me, and there I am, a ghost when desired, flesh when needed with the restless dead being no stranger and no fear. Ever eaten the dead? I can; just wait until your so thick-blooded you're straining to find the next Scale, the next Oath or agreement to keep yourself active. I'll be beside you supping on some lost soul unseen and sustained if mortals and animals no longer suffice in a pinch. Believe me, when I'm dragging them into the Land of Worms, having access to the restless dead -won't- be an issue.<br /> <br /> Don't worry; while your too busy worrying about the next experiment and going up the Sworn ladder, vying for empty thrones and puppet strings with the All Night Society, fucking around with gainless social experiments and rebellion, playing with your own blood and looking for a sign from some bastardized and stolen magics... I'll be in your haven. Waiting. When you close your eyes, I'll be there with my fangs in your flesh and my Convey's ready for their share. We'll pick who eats your soul once we're finished if it seems worthwhile before wandering back where living is just -comfortable- for a vampire.<br /> <br /> Covenant: Belial's Brood (yup). Faction: Tough to say. Likely a new minor one rather than something pre-established.<br /> <br /> Reasons: If you're a vampire, at some point you're going to have to come to terms with it and -accept it-. As much as I like the Ordo Dracul in particular and the others, none of them really present a means to both exist as what you truly are and remain -functional- as what you are, truly embracing it, truly exploring it's capabilities. The rest are either afraid, hiding or dabbling about, focusing on power alone, looking for mortal excuses, or simply going into denial and trying to change it before the even understand what &quot;it&quot; is.<br /> <br /> No. If I'm a vampire, I'm not dipping my toes into the pool for years and getting nowhere beyond trailblazing the same tepid path of wake, sleep, ennui, sleep, wake, become irrelevant, burn out. I'm going to be going into the deep end eventually and inevitably sooner or later. To hell with ennui, getting tired of mortal affairs, losing touch and blah blah blah, wah wah wah. With the Brood at least you have something more after that BS comes around. With the rest of the Covenants you just burn out pathetically, amounting to nothing because you can't reconcile what you are while preying upon the mortal herds. It's kind of sad, really. Running in circles.<br /> <br /> Even the Ordo are too busy shaking fists and patch jobs while pretty well ignoring some very fundamental things about vampirism. They like to see what the clay can be molded into, without looking at what the clay itself really is (because they have trouble adapting and contending with it). They ape what a lot of the Brood has already achieved, much like the Crones. Or so I'd think if I were Kindred. Measured approaches to something immeasurable. Bread and circuses to distract oneself. Hell, I might even have &quot;dabbled&quot; in the Ordo initially, developed a Coil or some scale before it got insufferable.<br /> <br /> Hell, even the territorial, lone predator shtick gets old: with the Brood you have a legitimate community with your Conveys that aren't just predicated on blood relations set in stone. Nope. The Brood offers more, just by heeding The Call. If I didn't do such early on, I sure as hell would have later after I got fed up with a vampire society that was just as much a farce as the human one I cam from.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Sta-Au: the Wicked and Cruel Ones. Go figure, while odd bedfellows they seem on the mark about quite a lot of things and they specifically survive in hostile areas. Besides which, they're one of the few endemic North American Bloodlines that may well exist where I live. Funny how that works out! Sure, you don't regain Humanity but... at that point it probably doesn't matter, and you sure as hell don't want to do that among the Brood as currently written anyhow.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex, Obfuscate, Protean, Resilience as per the Bloodline. Initial three dots will definitely end up Auspex 1, Obfuscate 1, Protean 1 and progress from there. possibly a touch of leftover Celerity from being Mekhet before getting tired of it all and wandering to a Land of Worms. Probably a bit of Animalism eventually later in unlife, possibly the earlier stages of a Coil (iffy, I doubt I'd be in the Ordo for the long haul) but certainly the Bloodline Devotions and Investments. So many directions, so many potentials over time and using Ghost Walk lets say hello to certain Numina and possibly Influences as well. Crazy, eh? Never know what I might pull out of undead sleeve.<br /> <br /> Walking by day? Oh woe... the angst of being denied such, I think I'll just... walk as a ghost! Or not worry about it when I'm back home among the Worms dragging your cherished mortals behind anyhow; did you know that sunlight is far less of an issue over there AND they're usually out of the way enough to be -not- worth others coming in? What are you going to do, send a band of nomads after me and my Convey on their home turf? Nah. Mortals? Feel free. Come in, take what I want, go back out while the others cower in gilded cages. Sounds great!<br /> <br /> Actually... please send some mortals after us! When they die they will be anchored there and doubly useful as feeding stock after death.<br /> <br /> Yep. I'd be a vicious, vicious monster, thrice over by Bloodline and Covenant. Odd how both appeal to me more in the long-term than the rest, but why fuck around? If it didn't start happening early, it sure would later. Vampiric society is like mortal society; full of near sociopathic assholes. Why not be the bigger one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T17:35:25-07:00","id":187538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=187512#post187512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan: Mekhet (irrelevant in part, see below)<br /> <br /> I won't be identifying myself as anything mo