please send some mortals after us! When they die they will be anchored there and doubly useful as feeding stock after death.<br /> <br /> Yep. I'd be a vicious, vicious monster, thrice over by Bloodline and Covenant. Odd how both appeal to me more in the long-term than the rest, but why fuck around? If it didn't start happening early, it sure would later. Vampiric society is like mortal society; full of near sociopathic assholes. Why not be the bigger one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Belgians.. they've made you so damn evil!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T06:30:38-07:00","id":187906,"title":"","content":"Clan - Nosferatu<br /> I wouldn't exactly describe myself as ugly or an outcast. But I do have troubles fitting in, especially in the bigger groups. I also have this natural aura of don't-talk-to-me.<br /> Other than that I'm socially not very strong, but I am a strong thinker and have the tendency to prank-scare people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Covenant - Invictus<br /> As a Nosferatu I'm a thinker. Thinking of how things could go better, but with the utmost respect for hierarchy. I don't wanna be top of the foodchain, but I don't like belonging to the lowbies either. So a midway in between, where the top of the foodchain people would care to listen to me, and the lowbies would want my advice on how to run things, and take my word for it.<br /> <br /> Bloodline - None<br /> I can't really think of a bloodline that suits me.<br /> <br /> Disciplines - Resilience 2, Celerity 1, Animalism 1, Auspex 1<br /> I can take a beating (and believe me I have) and I can run like the wind. Also if something falls, I'm one of the first to react and even sometimes catch it. Animalism 'cause animals and babies don't see my natural aura, and tend to come to me and enjoy my company. Auspex 'cause I usually notice alot about my environment. And most of the time when I say: &quot;Did you see that?&quot; the answer is No.<br /> <br /> Virtue - Justice<br /> I can't stand injustice, and it makes me freak out. At work this has given me the random problems, 'cause you know managers, they don't like being talked back to. Even if they know you're right.<br /> <br /> Vice - Sloth<br /> By the stars, I'm one lazy guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3073-tlrieslt","name":"tlrieslt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3073_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T17:50:42-07:00","id":188337,"title":"","content":"Clan - Mekhet<br /> <br /> While I think of myself as a likable enough guy, and I make friends easily enough, I have a tendency to get overwhelmed during social events and fade into the background. Plus, I'm fairly obsessed with weird stories and obscure trivia, and the idea of concealing myself with Obfuscate and poking around in hidden or restricted places appeals to me quite a bit. That and I'm kind of an Ancient Egypt nerd.<br /> <br /> Covenant - Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> It's unlikely that I'd rise terribly high, since I'm fairly squeamish about the kinds of things that hardcore Ordo researchers get up to, but if I were to become a vampire, I imagine that understanding my new condition as completely as possible would quickly become my first priority. Plus it's a good fit for my scholarly tendencies and my bloodline (see below). The Circle of the Crone appeals to me on a purely intellectual level, but I simply don't have the stomach for their particular variety of ritualism. The Lancea et Sanctum has its appeal as well, but being more-or-less and atheist I could never buy into their theology. Then again, if Dr. Caroline Petronius from <i>The </i><i>Testament of Longinus</i> can be a member of the covenant, maybe I could too.<br /> <br /> Bloodline - Agonistes<br /> <br /> As a history nerd and a student of anthropology, probably the most appealing thing to me about vampires in their connection to history and extinct cultures. Being able to interact with beings who could potentially tell the world so much that has otherwise been forgotten would be amazing, and the libraries and rituals of the Agonistes are resources too amazing for me to pass up.<br /> <br /> Disciplines - Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate<br /> <br /> I'd probably put one dot in each to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:06:14-07:00","id":189332,"title":"","content":"I would belong to the Macellarius bloodline, because I am an unabashed foodie and unfortunately morbidly obese; something I was made to believe was my defining characteristic while growing up in one of the most affluent (and consequently most svelte and surgically enhanced) areas of the USA. <br /> <br /> You'll forgive me if I don't cleave to your preferred format, but I believe that it makes the answers appear coldly compiled, which in turn detracts from the warmth and personality of these wonderful posts in which people describe themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T11:29:58-07:00","id":191551,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Mekhet<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Alucinor<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, and Cr\u00faac primarily likely with a dot of Celerity, Obfuscate, and Majesty as the blood thickens.<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons:</b><br /> When it comes to Clans in many ways I am split between the natures of the Daeva and Mekhet, inclined as I am toward both manipulation and subtlety, but I think in the end it is the method that has to be the deciding factor between them. I've always loved secrets and have somethign of an affinity for reading those around me, which is perhaps the core of my social skills, though from the responses I get I gather I'm fun to look at as well. Altering myself based on what I perceive others to desire is a natural inclination for me, and in a way that control over the extent of my presence has led to a certain skill at being unseen when I desire it. Together I think that's probably more than enough justification to tip things toward Shadow over Serpent. <br /> <br /> As for Covenants, I am a pagan, and the way the Circle was described in it's old Covenant book really made it fall into place for me. It is in my opinion the only path which can ever actually lead a vampire to reaching a state of peace with their own natures (excepting perhaps Golconda, but that's another matter entirely). I'm not sure how well I'd fair at learning Cr\u00faac via the whole 'torture the wisdom into you' method, but knowing you can recover perfectly from nearly any injury would probably help quite a bit, and if the slightly more cerebral methods implied in BS:S&amp;B are in effect then I'm perfectly content.<br /> <br /> The Alucinor, especially as remade for B&amp;S by Chris Falco are exceptionally attractive to me. The prophetic abilities they possess as well as the pervasive edge their influence gains from dreamweaving are major selling points for me, and I've always found dreams fascinating.<br /> <br /> Given how things have changed in B&amp;S its actually a struggle to decide how to assign things, but I suspect I'd have to start with at least 2 dots of Auspex and perhaps one of Cr\u00faac with a focus on divinatory and creation rites. The power to read secrets from a person's every move, and to control the foundations of the world are just too good to pass up. From there it would be pretty natural for me to develop a dot of Obfuscate, though it's unlikely I'd ever go much further, and one of Celerity if only for the sheer utility of it. Majesty would of course require a trainer, but it would make an excellent aid to feeding, and there's nothing quite like having all eyes on you as you move through a rave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3139-rayn-faustus","name":"Rayn Faustus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3139_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T12:13:38-07:00","id":191618,"title":"","content":"I think my favorite thing about this thread is getting to see everyone's takes on the Covenants and why they would chose to join them. I love seeing so many different perspectives on them, and these could all be good hooks for recruiting new members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T15:26:58-07:00","id":191730,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Daeva or Ventrue<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Anvari/Rotgrafen<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Probably focusing on perfecting Majesty and Nepenthe if Daeva, or if Ventrue maximizing Dominate and learning Majesty.<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons: </b>On one hand, I've always frequented the party scenes wherever I've lived, for better and for worse. It wouldn't be a stretch for me to end up as some degenerate Daeva. Ever hear of the books <i>The Doors of Perception </i>by Alduous Huxley and <i>Diary of a Drug Fiend</i> by Crowley? I'd end up trying to transcend the &quot;condition&quot; via the Ordo Dracul's Coils. Specifically those focusing on Blood and strengthening the will.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I'm of Swedish ancestry and would fit well into the Rotgrafen, what with being 6'4&quot; and fairly well read on Norse religions and customs. Couple that with the fact that I know how to sail, and I'd probably find my way into the Sea King's ranks. Provided, I'd end up flexing power in order to get the entirety of IKEA under my thumb, because what is more Nordic than IKEA? I'd send my rivals convoluted furniture for them to assemble and wait as they either frenzy, or die of supernatural blood pressure wrought from anger. The Ordo would still be the sect I'd go for, as transcendental improvement via the self is a core part of my life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T18:42:41-07:00","id":191884,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan: </b>Ventrue<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Lacea Sanctum or Carthians<br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Probably none<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Some mix of Dominate, Resilience, Obfuscate, Auspex, Theban Sorcery (if Lacea Sanctum)<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons:</b> I swim through bureaucracy like a fish to water. I'm never more comfortable than when I'm in a suit. I may not be the most appealing or intimidating person in the room, but I have a knack for knowing just what needs to be done and how to get everyone to do it the most official way possible. With the exception of my close friends I live on the fringes of any number of lives--always seeming to be available when needed, always close enough to hang out or call in a favor. I'm known for weathering brutal punishment physically and mentally and just never letting go of projects long after they should have died. Whether I joined the Lacea Sanctum or the Carthians would depend largely on whether I swallowed the former's connection to God. I'm deeply religious / spiritual, uncompromising at times, and draw my strength from that. On the other hand I have a zest for exploring different social structures and could see simply enjoying executing any number of Carthian experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T22:33:11-07:00","id":192031,"title":"","content":"Well apparently my use of a certain P-word got me banned for over a week without even giving me so much as a warning to change it. So I went back and edited it to avoid a similar incident in the future. Glad to see the topic and my post wasn't completely deleted while I was gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T05:37:22-07:00","id":192297,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Thing about the Clans is of course that they're supposed to be able to accomodate any character, but I think the most likely candidate is Ventrue (followed up by Mekhet and a Gangrel wish fullfilment).<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ordo Dracul or else Unbound<br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> I'm fine with vanilla flavoured ice cream<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> one dot in each, I'd probably enjoy Resillience and Animalism the most, though Dominate would come most natural to me<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons:</b>I'm not prepared so readily prepared to follow directives without question, so the Invictus is out. I am too cynical for a Carthian. Sanctified and Cronies I would fear, because - even with vampires being a real thing - the specifics of their beliefs would not make sense to me. (Also, magic is just too much of a hassle to learn to use properly.) I would be a natural fit for the Order, I more than enjoy regular academia and the Dragons are even able to physically manifest marks of their progressive transcendence. Yes, yes, so might witches and priests - but their kind of power is an allowance from something outside, it isn't a function of the activity of a vampire's own being. &quot;Spitting in God's face&quot; would, for me, mean: to demonstrate that the vampiric condition is a natural one (though that would not necessarily exclude God from the picture - Deus sive Natura and all that). However, if the local Dragons are greedy, fedora tipping, reductionist scientists or if they are priestly, free mason mystics, then I'd go Unbound.<br /> <br /> ... On second thought: I could live with a Gnostic strain of the Order, orchestrating major global events to bring about the demise of Yaldabaoth. A covenant of mad, Bene Gesserit eugeneticist sounds pretty sweet too.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Nyrufa: Seems a bit harsh, you sure you've not received warning for similar offenses in the past? Anyway, I enjoyed the thread, thanks for creating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T05:58:00-07:00","id":192308,"title":"","content":"Vampire isn't my favorite game. I like running it, but I wouldn't be so interested in playing it. I have a wife and child, so I wouldn't be that eager to go gallivanting off into the night.<br /> <br /> For the next ~16 years, I'd be that vampire so rare that I don't recall any mention of them beyond the Requiem core glossary. The Cleaver.<br /> <br /> Clan: Mekhet.<br /> Covenant: Unaligned/Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> This would be ideal, for me. I don't have the energy to be a gangrel anymore, nor the interest in attention to be daeva. While I'd love to just avoid notice, at the revelation of a supernatural world I'd want to know more, and coupled with my natural curiousity I'd want to dig up secrets everywhere. Nosferatu is probably the next most likely.<br /> <br /> I couldn't stand the court stuff, the politics stuff. I can run it, but I wouldn't want to play it. Outside of grabbing Dominate, my big priority would be keeping my family safe, and getting involved with that would make it really hard to do.<br /> Still, if I absolutely had to, or once the start was up, I'd probably be interested in joining the Circle of the Crone. I'm not a fan of the Church, or politics, or the pursuits of the Ordo Dracul. I suppose I might get the Call to join the Brood at some point in the far future (what's the point of being a monster of the night if you're not going to be an unholy monster of the night), but the Circle of the Crone would be a decent starter for me. Especially since I live in the Triangle, and apparently (according to B&amp;S) they're pretty open minded so I'd be able to find an angle I like to come at it.<br /> <br /> Ghoul the wife. Try to resist doing anything with the kid except encouraging them to do well in school (with dominate to help, 'do your homework', though 'go to sleep' would get a lot of use right now). My wife said she'd prefer being a hollow mekhet of the Ordo Dracul (she's more curious about other people than myself, and is a scientist), so by the time the kid was a good way to college we'd find a way to get that done. Probably make my neighborhood a hunting ground, have a quiet presence on the HOA. Justify my blood theft by solving their problems with the area.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Obfuscate, auspex, dominate. Eventually Blood Tenebrous, as I find the Spirit infinitely interesting and vampire-self wouldn't be able to avoid digging into the concept of another world when he found out about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-09-2014, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T07:39:44-07:00","id":192395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=187346#post187346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clan:</b> Ventrue<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons</b>: Would only be Ventrue simply for the Malkovian Bloodline. If I could, I would hands-down pick the old Malkavian however. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know the old Malkavians still exist as an unofficial bloodline, right? Its a condition that can effect every clan now, from Ventrue, to Gangrel, to Mekhet, to Nosferatu, and even the Daeva. As I understand it, they still retain the power to drive others mad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, I think I've finally decided on what possible Bloodlines I'd join. Going to go back and edit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:49:39-07:00","id":193876,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan: </b>Mekhet<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons:</b><br /> I've always been kind of a &quot;sit in the shadows and watch&quot; kind of a person. I feel like that would fit the Mekhet perfectly but it would also isolate me from the rest of any group ensuring that another Mekhet would isolate me and change me with relative ease. I'd likely stick close to my sire and feel more comfortable when around those of my own Clan not out of any real bonding with the community but that shared sense of self would make socialization (or not socializing) that much easier. so likely my clan would be pretty branded onto my identity.<br /> <br /> As for the Covenant, I drift towards the questions &quot;why&quot; and &quot;how&quot; way too much to feel mentally stimulated in any other covenant. Not that the damned condition would allow for those feelings to actualize but the Ordo Dracul would be the place where I could find someway to scratch the experimental itch.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline: </b>Mnemosyne<br /> <br /> I'd be too obsessed with having every bit of knowledge as I can. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:09:02-07:00","id":194061,"title":"","content":"Gangrel: I've always walked my own road even if it puts me at odd with the world around me. Plus I'm not afraid to get my hands dirty .<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul: I believe we should always strive to transcend who and what we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:05:25-07:00","id":195187,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Gangrel. I don't do well if I try to &quot;fit in&quot;\u2014never have, in fact\u2014and occasionally my temper overwhelms reason. When I snap, I <i><b>snap</b></i>. That, and I appreciate the idea of vampire-as-feral-thing (like the pack from <i>30 Days of Night</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Ordo Dracul. Screw doing the work of a God that hates you, or trying to make nice with a bunch of old spirits, or trying to play Illuminati. The Carthians have some merit (I tend to have a big thing for social justice and equality), but ultimately they feel like as soon as they'd gain power you'd just have an Invictus of another flavor. On the other hand, I like to be left alone to study, and learn more about... well, everything. Plus, I've always had a thing for transhumanity, so why wouldn't I want, well, transvampirism?<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b><b>: </b>Protean. Definitely. Someone asked me what I would wish for if I had a djinn's lamp, and I said 'biokinesis' (like the Trinity psi powers). I've always been fascinated with the idea of controlling my flesh, and besides, even if you had no haven, you'd always have shelter somewhere with Unmarked Grave. I also like dealing with animals more often than people at times, and I tend to be physically stubborn as well as mentally, so Animalism and Resilience are obvious too.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, a big draw to the Ordo is its Coils and Scales. The Coil of the Wyrm, especially, for controlling and unleashing the Beast at will. More of that, please. Other disciplines I'm not entirely sure of, but who wouldn't like a little Vigor or Obfuscate or Auspex or Majesty, to administer a better beatdown, or blend in the crowd, or pick out secrets, or be just that bit more charming?<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> This is the toughest question for me. Perhaps the Kerberoi, since I couldn't see myself as being the usual Gangrel hardass scourge or whatnot, I've never been the top dog but quite competent with being in the lead when I need to be, and sometimes, my behavior tends to ... have an effect on others around me. Or maybe I'd just found my own Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 07-11-2014, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:24:56-07:00","id":197971,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan: Ventrue</b><br /> <br /> I need to control my own path, I really love being free, and being free is about having the means to achieve such freedom no matter the odds. Although I am not good at playing the figurehead or to play the part as the boss people sometimes expect me to be, I always end up being a leader wherever I go.<br /> <br /> I am the person other people come to talk to when ideas are required, when there is a hard talk that must be had, when somebody needs to be convinced of something. I have grown a bit proud of being right all the time, and people rely on my opinions and on my judgement. Even when I am not (<i>de facto</i>) in charge people still expect me to lead and to find a proper way, especially in tough situations. I am the one to take the lead when others are scared, and I revel in going first and beating the unexpected. In a way, I believe that I can achieve more than what most can and the solitude that comes from it due to not having others who I can deem worth it, who can challenge me, who can complete me. That goes hand in hand with both the old <i>noblesse oblige</i> Ventrue and the <i>Aloof Curse </i>Ventrue. <br /> <br /> As I am a teacher, both in profession and speech, it is common for people to look for me for guidance. Especially newcomers and youngsters find a cosy environment around me. Many have deemed me unshakable and honourable, but a few have been able to see my manipulating the odds, and, shamelessly, trying to - and succeeding at - screwing anybody who has wronged me or those who are dear to me. There is always this ongoing debate of whether I am a kind, smiley, sympathetic soul or a manipulative SOB who everybody respects in front of others because they cannot defy simply because it is just hard to see what really affects me whereas, conversely, it seems to be very easy for me to hit people where it hurts when necessary.<br /> <br /> I guess being Ventrue would sit fine with me.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: Invictus</b><br /> <br /> I am reliable, and I tend to know a lot because I know how to approach people and both getting the information I want and making them believe they can count on me (and, usually, I really mean it). I do not wish to take on the mantle of leadership, it happens naturally when it happens, so those who want to wear the crown do not feel more than somewhat threatened by me, and they end up needing my aid. I do not follow commands just because they are orders, but I know how to question and - what is better - questioning somebody else's leadership and orders in a way that will not leave the figurehead exposed... I like whispering in the ears of those who honestly want to wear the crown and occupy the throne while I am the one calling the actual shots and being the one the normal folks look up to, and the one whose guidance the actual leader cannot live without. That grants me the freedom I like so much, and guarantees that I will only be bothered by the things which are more interesting and not so boring.<br /> <br /> Also, I do not believe in utopia. I do believe that organisation is essential. I think that power comes naturally to those who have the means to seize it, and good things will come when somebody is worth it. Crying for equality and justice when life is unfair to begin with is utterly pointless. Adapting and playing the system is the best way to be ultimately free.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline: None.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: Auspex, Dominate, Resilience, Celerity.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/808-tempus","name":"Tempus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T19:37:42-07:00","id":201726,"title":"","content":"My turn. <br /> CLAN: Mekhet primarily. Possibly Gangrel, Daeva ONLY if I get to be a Septim(See Bloodline) <br /> REASON: The Shadows are my sort of people. They're quiet, value learning, and aren't the most social. Which, funnily, is why I didn't want the Haunts; I'm bad enough being social as is. The enduring strength of the Gangrel is tempting, and I can often get angry to rather extreme levels. Ventrue are aristocratic in ways that raise my hackles('MERICA!), and I'm far too much a prude to be your average Daeva. <br /> <br /> COVENANT: Ordo Dracul, NO EXCEPTIONS. <br /> REASON: I cannot stress this enough. The Carthians are well meant, but they target the symptoms rather than the disease. Invictus are what our ancestors threw tea in the harbor to be rid of, and I'm a Christian, so the Circle is right out(not that I'd hate them, though I'd probably have to watch out for Cruac after one &quot;Will you acept Jesus as your lord and Savior?&quot; Too many). Which brings me to the Sanctum. I hate them SO. VERY. MUCH! They are the ultimate Blasphemy, and they are the agents of the very damnation they claim to prevent. The Ordo is, in my opinion, the only sane, moral way to react to being forced into a monster that goes around hurting people to survive. But even then, the Ordo is just the least of all evils. They are rather antagonistic to the divine, and promote truly horrific practices in the name of change(Counting the Dragon's Scales, anyone?). Yet, to deny them is to, in some way, accept hurting others to survive. The Coil of Blood alone could save hundreds of lives. The only way to reconcile these facts would be to become some sort of radical reformer, a dangerous, likely futile proposal, but it is the only option I can stomach. And really, is a world with one less vampire worse off?<br /> <br /> BLOODLINE:None/Septim <br /> REASON: None of the Gangrel or Mekhet Bloodlines appeal to me. But the Septim, despite being Daeva, resonate with me like no other bloodline. Genuine Christians who hate the Sanctum and have the literal power to protect people from supernatural hoodo? Sign me up! <br /> <br /> DISCIPLINES: Auspex is a big one. What you don't know can kill you in your sleep, after all(speaking of which, Obscufate is also a needed thing). Protean provides many very useful tricks, and Coils are such a must have they go without saying. If a Septim, then Abjuration is top priority(save afor-mentioned coils). Others get smatterings of as useful. Except Majesty, Majesty is just one big slippery slope waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Some very valid concerns over my choice of covenant. 07-19-2014, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T20:03:33-07:00","id":201734,"title":"","content":"I should address this sometime.<br /> <br /> @Zeal: You do know that the Ordo encourage fairly cruel experimental procedures on Kindred and humans alike, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T08:45:41-07:00","id":202172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=201734#post201734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should address this sometime.<br /> <br /> @Zeal: You do know that the Ordo encourage fairly cruel experimental procedures on Kindred and humans alike, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully. I understand my strong faith(in a Covenant whose founder's goal could be defined as &quot;Defy God&quot;) and my refusal to violate my ethics in the name of SCIENCE(!) would likely make me a low status &quot;friend nobody likes&quot;, but the goal of the Ordo as a whole are the best for both humans and vampires alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:00:11-07:00","id":202192,"title":"","content":"<b>What to List:</b><br /> <br /> Clan Ventrue<br /> <br /> Covenant Unaligned maybe Carthains<br /> <br /> Reasons:I'm highly idealistic despite not being as vocal as many others. Ventrue because I'm Ventrue. Malocusian because if I have the option I would never leave my room or my home. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional Listing:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodline Malocusians<br /> <br /> Disciplines Resillience Domus Dominate Nightmare","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:05:55-07:00","id":202194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=202172#post202172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully. I understand my strong faith(in a Covenant whose founder's goal could be defined as &quot;Defy God&quot;) and my refusal to violate my ethics in the name of SCIENCE(!) would likely make me a low status &quot;friend nobody likes&quot;, but the goal of the Ordo as a whole are the best for both humans and vampires alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>You violated your so-called Christian ethics the moment you joined an organization who's stated mission openly blasphemes against God's supreme divinity and actively works to supplant him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T09:43:01-07:00","id":202208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=202194#post202194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You violated your so-called Christian ethics the moment you joined an organization who's stated mission openly blasphemes against God's supreme divinity and actively works to supplant him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is that. The Covenant quote is &quot;I will in the eye of God. And he will allow it&quot;.They openly call God insane and senile.<br /> <br /> The Invictus and and the Carthians are the only ones who don't violate a solid Christian devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T10:41:17-07:00","id":202239,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan: </b>Nosferatu<br /> <br /> So I've mentioned in the Werewolf and Changeling threads that I am most likely a Cahalith and would most likely be taken and shifted into a Darkling. Both are true, and Vampire oddly illustrates it best with the fact I'd be a Nosferatu. I wouldn't say that of the x-splats the Nossies represent me best-if anything a Fairest Shadowsoul might do that best, and the only reason I don't put more in that is the way I'd react in Fairest conditions, off the side tangent now Arc- but they are surprisingly good in the mix of noise and silence. When I want your attention, I'll get it. When I want to fade into the background, it may be a little more work but I can do that work easily enough. I also have a macabre streak, and an emphasis on never neglecting, denying the ugly parts of life-on a positive spin I make a point of looking at the ugly to find something beautiful and uplifting about it, which doesn't hurt the Nossies. Point is that the creepy, the dark, and the horrific have a place in my hands and in my life. Unsurprisingly, that does make me a bit of an outsider, and I have lost track of the number of times I felt like the outsider looking in.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>The Carthian Movement<br /> <br /> Truth be told, while I enjoy several covenants as a player, I'm less thrilled with the prospect of personally joining them. Still, it's hard to deny the benefits they offer, and employment beats being unaligned on a lot of fronts-at least someone should theoretically care if the hunters smear my face on the wall. Still, why the Carthians? I'm not politically minded, and what little I am leans towards moderation between two sides. I'm not sure that vampire society <i>needs</i> the sort of revolution they talk about. So why them? Well, first off, change as a principle. I'm not sure if the popular modus operandi of vampires is the right way for it to work, but I can definitely say that even if it largely works there are details that definitely need work. Even if it doesn't, someone needs to be asking the questions, re-evaluating what works and what doesn't. I'm a natural devil's advocate, and even if I don't want to overthrow the current model, I'm definitely willing to challenge it and see if it deserves to stand. Second, Negotiation. The Carthians occupy a neat niche where they can actually mediate for all the other covenant-they aren't exactly a neutral party, but they can certainly have members who can be, and I can very easily be one of those people-hell, I am. My willingness to question and work for a better answer mixed in with this aspect of the Carthians means I could live quite happily trying to work the angles of society to get them to work better. I might be a softcore revolutionary, but simply put their need to challenge and improve society appeals to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Majesty 3, Nightmare 4, Auspex, Vigor 5, Celerity 5, Obfuscate 3<br /> <br /> Before I even touch on the Nosferatu powers, I'd have to learn at least some of Majesty. I'm sorry, I'm vain. I'm selfish. To be able to live in the spotlight? To get attention? Sign me up. I'm not sure how far I'd go with it though. Getting your foot in the door is one thing, and creating inclinations to like you is okay, but how far do I go before I feel like I'm really just violating people? I want a hand up, not a hand holding everyone's heart.<br /> <br /> Of the Nossie powerset I'd probably go with Vigor...maybe not first, but definitely fullest. I'm not very strong in real life, and that has always bothered me a little bit. I don't build muscle easily, either, so to magically become more potent is appealing. The vast amount I could do with that is nifty, plus it's the least ethically challenging. I think for that reason Nightmare would also grow a lot-truth be told, I don't really want to hurt people, and if I could just get people to back down, that would be lovely. Of course, there's a line to be drawn-how far do you scare a person before you're being unfair, before it becomes cruel? Still, Nightmare would probably grow a lot, even if I felt guilty about some of the higher power. Obfuscate is the first one I thought I'd raise high as possible, and the first one I immediately back down. Just as I want the ability to grab people's attention, positively or negatively, I also want the ability to just disappear. But do I want to really be invisible? Do I need the temptation of invisible knives and guns? I have no problem lying to people, but words are different from looking like the person others want to see most-could I really trust myself with that power. I couldn't resist building it up, but I'd be five kinds of worried about doing wrong with it.<br /> <br /> So onto something a little lighter, I love speed. I love velocity, I love going fast. I get <i>ecstatic</i> at high speeds. Add in Vigor's addition to distance to throw in freefall, and good lord I might get shot for breaching the masquerade just by freerunning. Still, how could I resist?!<br /> <br /> Auspex has some clearer lines of use for me than the other morally ambiguous powers. I debate Majesty, Nightmare, and Obfuscate at the third dot(maybe even earlier), but Auspex clearly cuts off after that. I'm fairly good at reading people and scenarios, but it never hurts to know more. Still, of the six I'd seek after, Auspex is probably the one I'd go after the least-while I as a player love it, I wouldn't be as crazy about it in life, and quite frankly the entire thing would probably just make me uber paranoid, and I don't want to be <i>that</i> guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T13:08:17-07:00","id":202329,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, vampire society probably couldn't function without the Carthians. Imagine the modern day American fledgling. He's been raised in a society where he's given a great deal of freedom and allowed to speak his mind. Then one night he's embraced and finds some 300 year old prince wants him to bend knee and kiss his ring like it's the fucking Renascence. You'd have to be insane to think somebody raised in modern human society is going to flip the switch and go back to the dark ages over night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still that being said, Blood Magic is awesome, so I'd still go with the Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T14:21:23-07:00","id":202366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=202329#post202329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, vampire society probably couldn't function without the Carthians. Imagine the modern day American fledgling. He's been raised in a society where he's given a great deal of freedom and allowed to speak his mind. Then one night he's embraced and finds some 300 year old prince wants him to bend knee and kiss his ring like it's the fucking Renascence. You'd have to be insane to think somebody raised in modern human society is going to flip the switch and go back to the dark ages over night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that this reaction is the reason the Carthians exist, not vice versa. I mean, what would these Neonates do if there were no Carthian movement? Rebel against their tyrannical elders? Maybe, but an individual childe would have no chance against an ancient Prince in open conflict. The oppressed younger generation would have to organize, to form a unified rebellion. A movement, if you will. But what to call this group of freedom fighters? Hmm...<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, I see the Carthian movement as less of the glue that holds Kindred society together, and as more of a natural reaction to the state that society is in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T14:33:32-07:00","id":202393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=202329#post202329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, vampire society probably couldn't function without the Carthians. Imagine the modern day American fledgling. He's been raised in a society where he's given a great deal of freedom and allowed to speak his mind. Then one night he's embraced and finds some 300 year old prince wants him to bend knee and kiss his ring like it's the fucking Renascence. You'd have to be insane to think somebody raised in modern human society is going to flip the switch and go back to the dark ages over night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still that being said, Blood Magic is awesome, so I'd still go with the Circle of the Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joy of being a Carthian these days-you can join other groups as well. Be an interesting choice between the Circle and the Ordo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:47:01-07:00","id":208774,"title":"","content":"I have lost a massive amount of weight and would like to change my answer to 'baggy daeva'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T00:32:49-07:00","id":209172,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: <i>Want </i>to be Daeva. Because duh.<br /> <i>Would </i>be either Mekhet or Nosferatu- on the one hand, I'm cold and empty and into knowing while being unknown; on the other, I'm an (anti)popular dedicated loner who likes to freak people out and have a talent for accidentally sneaking up on the unsuspecting.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Either Unaligned (because most other kindred are either assholes or zealots, and also I'm super lazy without something super interesting to catch my attention) or Ordo, if I could get over what tiny bit of squeam I have left (because <i>holy shit vampires and werewolves and blood magic and fuck your absentee landlord god aaaagh study catalogue investigate</i>). Carthians if I were <i>really</i> compelled to get political (not to mention the idea of synergizing kindred with modern technology appeals to my inner min-maxer) but never ever Circle or Sanctified because the one constant of the Blood seems to be how infinitely mutable it is, which kind of runs counter to their absolute conviction about <i>what</i> and <i>how</i> and especially <i>why</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline</b>: Eh. That one that makes Nosferatu pretty, maybe? Hollow would be appropriate, I guess, but I'd never want to be one because I'd have to deal with my own pissy ghost, and I'm adept enough at inventive unpleasantness <i>as is, </i>thank you<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: I already have a not-so-subtle lean towards Nightmare and Obfuscate, and a better-than-average rapport with animals would indicate low Animalism. Auspex would be hit or miss; I'm either distressingly insightful or stunningly oblivious. I've always valued speed over strength or stamina, so Celerity would be fun on a bun (also PARKOOOOOUR!!). I'd go <i>way</i> out of my way to learn a little Dominate just for the sheer utility, and way <i>WAY</i> out of my way to learn Majesty because <i>Goddamn it I WILL learn to club before I die</i> ):-(<br /> <br /> Despite my cynicism and general lack of regard for people, I would probably either adjust poorly to the exploitative, combative kindred lifestyle and make a sad, clumsy vampire, or be <i>way too good</i> at it and draugr in a few months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 07-26-2014, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T04:28:25-07:00","id":209990,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: <b>Nosferatu</b><br /> <br /> This is an interesting one for me. Because, to be blunt about myself; while on the surface I am all smiles and joy, under my skin I am <i>fully </i>aware of how manipulative I can be. I know what words to say and what I can do to get <i>exactly </i>what I want - and more than that, I've gotten it down to a very fine art and I know that it <i>works</i>. I am often the one people come to if they need support and I am the one most often told secrets to because of this. I am not so quiet and withdrawn as to be a Mekhet, however - and the likes of ancient history and forbidden knowledge would have little interest to me. Certainly not enough to make a Requiem out of. Which then turns me towards The Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> While yes I am social, I am only social to the point I <i>wish </i>to be. Neither am I squeamish about gore (except eyes and nails &gt;&gt;) or the darker parts of existence. If people knew more of me I would likely be a social outcast rather than the somewhat-butterfly I truly am (due to hobbies and the like). And yet the idea of <i>knowing </i>things and having leverage is deeply appealing - but again, not in the same way it is for a Mekhet. If I had the choice I would be unchanged from how I am now - my Curse would be an aura of <i>weird</i> less than any deformity. To be frank, for all I am not exactly a beautiful person I <i>am </i>currently capable of acting in society. I'd like that to continue, even if I make people uneasy.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: <b>Unaligned</b><br /> <br /> For all I play many characters whom are fine with the Covenants, none of them truly stand out as something I would wish to join. I am at heart a survivor - enough not to put myself in the firing line by attacking the system with the Carthians or being the pawn of some Invictus Elder whom does not care for my life. Neither am I religious - on either end - and I would not wish to meddle too much in The Dragons less I mess something up for myself.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline</b>: <b>None</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: <b>Animalism 3, Vigor 4, Nightmare 4, Obfuscate 3, Celerity 2</b><br /> <br /> So these are fairly straight forward for me; Animalism is because I love animals. I'd probably not go too far into the tree if only because talking to them, being able to command them if needs must and summon them to my aid. That and, well, it's always good to have pets!<br /> <br /> Vigor because, unfortunately, my muscles in real life are poor. I suffer from some conditions which weaken my joints and have messed my muscles up. The idea of having the strength to rip a man in two is rather intoxicating. It would let me do things I could never do in life - and, if I <i>have </i>to fight, beat the other guy to the point he doesn't try again!<br /> <br /> Nightmare... well, it's useful. As I have said, I can manipulate to get my own way but I have never been one to manipulate someone in that way. I hope I never would - this would, again, be nothing more than insurance. That if you come after me, I can break your mind in two - it is either <i>me </i>or <i>you </i>and I will never chose you over my own life. Just as I'd quickly learn not to do with other Kindred.<br /> <br /> What better way of gathering information and getting around than simply being invisible? Being able to hide things is a wonderful gift - or stalk people and break their necks, if I had to. I'd prefer not to, but again everything has a reason.<br /> <br /> And finally, celerity. To put it simply; I can get the hell out of dodge quickly. Or close in on someone. It'd vary, I imagine!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T05:38:39-07:00","id":210036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mabs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=209990#post209990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clan</b>: <b>Nosferatu</b><br /> <br /> This is an interesting one for me. Because, to be blunt about myself; while on the surface I am all smiles and joy, under my skin I am <i>fully </i>aware of how manipulative I can be. I know what words to say and what I can do to get <i>exactly </i>what I want - and more than that, I've gotten it down to a very fine art and I know that it <i>works</i>. I am often the one people come to if they need support and I am the one most often told secrets to because of this. I am not so quiet and withdrawn as to be a Mekhet, however - and the likes of ancient history and forbidden knowledge would have little interest to me. Certainly not enough to make a Requiem out of. Which then turns me towards The Nosferatu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds Daeva to me. Pretending at joy and socializing? Actually being a manipulator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:07:58-07:00","id":210044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=210036#post210036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds Daeva to me. Pretending at joy and socializing? Actually being a manipulator?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I think of the Cockscomb Society, I imagine two Nosferatu in fancy suits (with monacles) listening to Mozart while they politely drink blood out of tea cups together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:12:56-07:00","id":210058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=210036#post210036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds Daeva to me. Pretending at joy and socializing? Actually being a manipulator?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I considered the Daeva first. But the difference is, I actually ENJOY socializing. It's not a front and I have never used my knowledge to hurt others - especially not those I care about. I value those around me as much as I do my family. When I say I manipulate, it's more in the sense that I can be <i>very </i>persuasive than flat-out manipulation. I am, so I have been told, gifted with words. So other than the possibility of using what I know against people, I don't feel I fit the Daeva outside of that. I don't like being the centre of attention, I don't enjoy the nightlife and I certainly don't want to put myself in the spotlight ^^ All of the social spitting that typically follow Daeva just... isn't me!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","user":"Mabs","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T00:53:09-07:00","id":213273,"title":"","content":"Clan: Mekhet or Ventrue<br /> I'm a lurker, a lingerer on the outside edge, but when I want to be heard I am. I speak publicly without issue, it is the small talk stuff that I don't get. Lords and Shadows aren't known for their small talk, but they are known for making an impact when they do speak. I've stopped rooms from arguing with a single, forceful word. This being said, I'm an outsider mroe often than not. I was never part of the &quot;In-crowd&quot;, or have ever really felt welcome and comfortable anywhere. If I'm not being ignored, I'm often used for information and then forced right back into obscurity. I'm Observant, especially when it comes to body language and background information. I lean towards Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Covenant: Carthian<br /> I am a huge follower, arguer and debater of politics. I know enough that I can argue almost any side of a debate, and do so very well. What is universal though is my hatred for the way things are, and how calmly people just accept the things it forces on them. I could go for hours ranting about teachers who can't pay rent while some dumb as a rock celebrity makes a multi-million dollar sex-tape. I grew up poor, and plight of the neonates against the glass ceiling of age sounds like the perfect cause to sign up for. When debating, I sometimes get so fired up that any topic becomes fair game, religion, politics, social policy, feminist theory. Could you imagine it, a Kindred at a &quot;Take Back the Night Walk&quot;? Making Religious leaders admit to their illicit activities? As a Carthian I would right the wrongs, and burn those too stubborn to see reason.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Mnemosyne, I can already recall whole pages of text after a few glances anyway. None if Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Dominate 3, Obfuscate 3.<br /> The invisible, unperceived threat combined with the power to shut down memories? Yes, please! Be in any room, hear any conversation and then use it to fuel the Cause? More, More! Turn a Kine fat cat into a penniless bum with a handful of words, and then vanish from sight and memory? This is just <i>too</i> good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T11:54:16-07:00","id":216065,"title":"","content":"Clan: Mekhet<br /> <br /> Covenant: Lancea Sanctum<br /> <br /> Reasons: I'd love being more of a night person and I wouldn't mind being a spy. Lancea Sanctum would be the covenant for me because it would take the least amount of changing my views on things. I'd be a Carthian but I'm too pessimistic to believe that the person I'd want to have in charge of my domain would ever be democratically elected. I'd be uncomfortable at the first few sermons I attended but I'm sure after a few months I'd get over it.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 4 &amp; Obfuscate 3 because invisibility and mind reading are some of my favorite super powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1244-starsoverstalingrad","name":"StarsOverStalingrad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1244_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T23:23:36-07:00","id":216534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/185837-what-kindred-would-you-be?p=189332#post189332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would belong to the Macellarius bloodline, because I am an unabashed foodie and unfortunately morbidly obese; something I was made to believe was my defining characteristic while growing up in one of the most affluent (and consequently most svelte and surgically enhanced) areas of the USA.<br /> <br /> You'll forgive me if I don't cleave to your preferred format, but I believe that it makes the answers appear coldly compiled, which in turn detracts from the warmth and personality of these wonderful posts in which people describe themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah Andrew, I was starting to miss you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T10:26:00-08:00","id":1022386,"title":"","content":"Rise from your grave!<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Ventrue <br /> This is at first an odd choice for me because outside of my job, or scripted acting, I find myself to be a bit socially awkward and impatient. I neglect friends that I make in real life because I have other interests they have nothing to do with. But then I realized just how horrifying that makes becoming a Ventrue for me in all the right ways. I'd get a little more Resolve, meaning I would become more patient and focused, while simultaneously being inducted into a line of power that allows me to bypass many of the social niceties and uncertainties life has to offer. I can simply demand what I desire from others, and I will receive it.<br /> <br /> It's wonderful. I get to win so hard now, get to take what I want and nobody can hope to stop me. It's terrible, because it feeds into the worst of my foibles by creating shortcuts that weren't there before. And worst of all it just makes me even more distant than I already am from the people in my life; my Touchstones would feel so neglected. <br /> <br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ordo Dracul.<br /> I am already a bit of a maltheist to begin with - if God exists it's either incompetent or malicious, etc etc. Becoming a vampire and then having some vampires tell me this is the case would be pretty interesting. Having them demonstrate that they've made tangible improvements on the vampire condition would win me over pretty much immediately. Because I really think being a vampire can be something great if you just overcome some of the weaknesses involved with it.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the wicked mad scientist stuff might put me off at first. But I think in all likelihood my objections there wouldn't last long when I'm a vampire, especially when tangible results reveal themselves as products of whatever awfulness is done. I will achieve praxis over my own body as I do over the people around me!<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> I'm honestly not sure here. I might make up my own if my blood gets potent enough. If I had to pick an existing one I might be one of the Sons of Cade. I have a real bad temper on top of my other issues, and it fits into my preferred fourth Discipline anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Coils of the Wyrm, Dominate, Resilience, Vigor.<br /> I love having animals around, and I've often wished I could have them understand me and vice versa when I speak to them. More importantly I would like for them to do what I tell them to. The same thing with people, really; this is part of that &quot;winning&quot; thing for me. Plus I want to be nearly indestructible and strong enough to break free of any bindings others put me in, just in case assuming direct control doesn't work and I need to defend myself. Besides, I was never very physically inclined to begin with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T12:56:13-08:00","id":1022427,"title":"","content":"Why not?<br /> <br /> Clan: Nosferatu<br /> I'm already the slightly weird and creepy guy who's surprisingly stealthy for my size (and if I'm being honest with myself, I get a little thrill from how people react when I sneak up on them) and feels like I blend into the background in most social situations. Perfect fit, really. If I can feed without my dinner or anyone else even knowing I was ever there, then I've done it right. If I stumble across some asshole who &quot;deserves&quot; to get the blood sucked out of 'em, then I scare the crap out of them before going in for a bigger bite than usual.<br /> <br /> Covenant: Unaligned, or somewhere between the Carthian Movement and the Lancea et Sanctum<br /> To be fair, Vampire is not my favorite supernatural or gameline, so I'm not the sort who would actually choose to be embraced. So if I'm joining the All Night Society, it's unwillingly. That being said, eternity is a long time, and eventually I'd probably need to make some friends and/or get some structure in my nights. Carthian if I decided to dip my toes in the political side, Lance if I end up hitting &quot;fuck it&quot; and wade into the deeper end of being a monster.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: None<br /> Like I said, I'm not all that into Vampire, so A) I wouldn't really know what I ought to choose for the best kewl powaz, and B) I can't see myself wanting to join a Bloodline in any case unless my sire is part of one and I have no choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Obfuscate and Nightmare to start, getting into Vigor and other physical Disciplines like Celerity and Resilience later, possibly looking for someone willing to teach me a little Auspex at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:38:18-08:00","id":1022721,"title":"","content":"Let's see here...<br /> <br /> <b>Clan: </b>Mekhet (or less likely, Daeva)<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Carthian Movement<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons: </b>I have a talent for making people do what I want, even though I'm not exactly assertive or forceful in my demands. With time and practice I could be a diplomat between Covenants for the Carthians, as I don't see myself as a promising member of any other covenant (save maybe for the Ordo Dracul).<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>For the initial three dots: Auspex 2, Majesty 1<br /> <br /> This thread has been dead for quite a while, let's rise it again shall we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:07:38-08:00","id":1022762,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan:</b> Daeva. Because I'm a bloody passionate person.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Probably Toreador with the weakness tied to movies and tv shows. Because I'm quite a lover of the screen, both big and small.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Invictus / Ordo Dracul (mystery of the ascendant or zirnitra) / Circle of the Crone (depending on the cult) with Invictus as the major covenant. Invictus because I'm a join-the-establishment-and-get-power type (currently in law school), Ordo Dracul because I'd want to get past the weaknesses of the vampiric condition and I've always been interested in the sciences, even if the Ordo is a bit strange with their approach and finally the Circle because at least with the typical version of them I wouldn't have to make too much of a modification of my own religious beliefs and because Cruac (at least if the Themes version is used).<br /> <br /> <b>Initial Disciplines: </b>Majesty 2, Cruac 1 with a focus on gaining Coils, Dominate, and the physical disciplines as time goes on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T20:35:27-08:00","id":1023090,"title":"","content":"Clan: Mekhet; I'm a bookish type that likes to stick in the background and watch.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Probably the Brothers of Ypres because I love their ties to World War 1, and I love that they're vampires who typically wander around a lot.<br /> <br /> Covenant: Unaligned. I'd be unaligned because of said nomadic tendencies.<br /> <br /> Initial Disciplines: Obfuscate Two and Auspex One, with a focus on mastering my clan and bloodline disciplines as time goes on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:41:38-08:00","id":1023268,"title":"","content":"Clan: Daeva<br /> <br /> I typically prefer the concept of vampires as an 'alive, but different' mix of physical powerhouse and social god, and among the VtR Clans, the Daeva seem to come the closest to this ideal. Their zest for life aligns with my own and their specialty abilities seem the most suited to my tastes, especially if you use a Bloodline that grants Dominate as a specialty Discipline, even more so than the Ventrue or the Gangrel. My only gripe with the Clan is their Weakness seems very little aligned with my personality (I generally need some serious, extended involvement to start feeling attached to a person, and need little effort to cope with breakups and personal losses). In terms of Clan Weaknesses, the Ventrue or the Mekhet seem rather more suited to my personality (I'm an aloof, analytic person, if a cheerful, can-do one), but since their specialty abilities appeal less to me (I have scarce interest for stealth, divination, telepathy, or influence over animals), I fancy the notion of 'as alive as possible' vampires, and I have a choice, I'd prefer to pick the Daeva, and try by other means (such as the Coil of Ziva) to minimize the effects of their freakish curse.<br /> <br /> Covenant: Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> I am very much invested in transhumanism and the notion of indefinite self-improvement, and after the Embrace, this would almost surely translate into a strong interest and affinity for the ideals and practices of the Ordo Dracul. On the other hand, I also find considerable appeal in the supernatural and the notion of magical control over reality, so I'd almost surely find significant interest in blood magic as well. I'm a secular, pro-science person with little sympathy for organized religion, even less if it is of the judgemental kind. Overall I'd find myself rather more at ease with the ideals and practices of the Acolytes than the Sanctified, even if I'd try and give Cruac a spin as immanent and impersonal as possible. Since I admire generalist polymaths and immortality would thankfully give me indefinite time to purse non-specialization, dual Covenant seems the best choice here, with Ordo Dracul as the primary affiliation and Circle of the Crone as the secondary one.<br /> <br /> I acknowledge the material benefits of the political Covenants, but typically I find them less appealing than the mystical ones of the ideological Covenants, and both the strong hierarchical bent of the Invictus and the far-left revolutionary activism of the Carthians turn me off. Theoretically speaking, I might find a few trade secrets of the Carthians appealing enough to try and pursue tertiary affiliation among them (especially since their practices may minimize the social costs of such cosmopolitanism), but I'd still face the issue of my considerable antipathy for their ideological roots. Then again, I might be practical-minded and opportunist enough to fake interest in their ideology well enough to grab the boons I'm really interested in.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Toreador<br /> <br /> Since I'm a perfectionist person, and very much interested in getting Dominate as a specialty Discipline alongside Celerity, Majesty, and Vigor, I'd pick Toreador as Bloodline, with the caveat that my personal version of their ideal would focus my urge and admiration for 'artistic' excellence on something like martial arts, fencing, athletics, software development, and/or theoretical science. I am a creatively-challenged person with little affinity, talent, or interest for fine or high arts. So I'd have to find an Avus that is open-minded to my version of the Bloodline ideal (the Founder was a bullfighter, so it seems it should not be that difficult), or bargain/steal/trick my way into their blood.<br /> <br /> Disciplines<br /> <br /> I would be strongly interested into most of them and pursue a generalist approach to their development, with a broad ideal of balance between physical enhancement, mental manipulation, shapeshifting, blood sorcery, and overcoming of vampiric limitations. So I'd certainly strive to master Celerity, Cruac, the Coils of the Dragon, Dominate, Majesty, Protean, Resilience, and Vigor. In all likelihood Nightmare as well to round up my arsenal of mind manipulation powers, which I'd find very useful to deal with my feeding needs and protect my unlife (when the soft approach fails, that what's the combat Disciplines are for). I'd probably ignore or neglect Animalism, Auspex, and Obfuscate, unless perhaps I repeatedly find myself in circumstances that make them exceedingly useful. I'd find Cruac rather more congenial a version of blood sorcery than Theban Sorcery. I'd deem pretty much all the Coils of the Dragon rather interesting and useful for different reasons (except for temporary return to mortality and building an army of blood-bonded thralls). I'd likely use the Coil of Zirnitra to develop a few telekinetic and psychokinetic abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-05-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:36:47-08:00","id":1023867,"title":"","content":"Clan: Ventrue. I must admit that I am an arrogant person, who have a tendency to instability and a real problem with maintaining long term relationships. Feeling &quot;detached&quot; an &quot;aloof&quot; are everyday feelings for me, together with a strong need to show how &quot;good&quot; I am. Plus, I have a bit of obsession with things like nobility and royalty, so it just feels natural (as being a vampire may be, that is).<br /> <br /> Covenant: Weihan Cynn, if possible- Ordo Dracul if not. While the Invictus does looks alluring, being a winner is not exactly my greatest strength, and power for its own sake would make me bored in a sort time. The Weihan Cynn, on the other hand, feel a lot more natural- from one side, they have their control over politics, being used as neutral parties and maintaining a network of alliances and connections is something that comes to me almost naturally, and my regular interest in the occult world more as &quot;watching from the background&quot; and less about actually practicing them in the form of blood sorcery of some kind. In case I can't choose them, I'll go with the second best- which is the Ordo Dracul, as my scientific interests and my own tendency to always &quot;push against my limits&quot; would draw me there over any other covenant.<br /> <br /> Bloodline: Dragolescu. Again, an outcome of my interest in the occult and the &quot;world beyond&quot; together with the looming prophesy and the general distrust the population have around them just makes sense- not to mention their inability to find satisfaction in the little things, turning them &quot;restless&quot; as their curse mentions.<br /> <br /> Initial Disciplines: Dominate and Auspex (I consider that to be the Dragolescu's Bloodline Discipline in 2E), plus at least 1 dot at Majesty (I have a certain amount of magnetic presence when I want to). Animalism would definitely won't be one of them (I like animals, they don't like me. Perhaps some sort of a Bane or something), and I would probably won't have high (or any) dots on the Physicals. If I'll be in the Ordo, I assume I'll have some dots at the Coils- but not a lot, as I do not try on myself anything hastily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:48:22-08:00","id":1024870,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: You don't get to pick clan; the clan picks you. In general, I think I'd end up Mekhet if scouted, but Venture if I could pick or was the object of competition. However, as it depend solely on my sire, you never know. I can see a potential reason for every clan wanting me, and another for every clan rejecting me. Dominate is hands down my preferred discipline though.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: I would likely find myself in the Invictus first. I'd want to understand each group and as the Invictus offer a generic 'we are a commonwealth with no requirements', I might end up there. Going it unaligned wouldn't make sense to neonate Tabanese. Thing is, this initial recruitment might be enough for me to STAY in the Invictus even after seeing the others. Only extreme dissatisfaction with the Invictus or extreme attraction to the Carthians would have me change political allegiance and the Ordo would have to present as the 'university' of vampire society to grab my attention in the first place. If they didn't, they'd be lumped in with the religious cults and dismissed.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline</b>: Lynx if Mekhet and Masons if Venture would be mechanical picks, but to be honest, I'd likely shy away from committing to a bloodline, especially if I felt I could create one.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: I think all the disciplines and the devotions I could create would interest me. I'd find a great deal of joy probing the Beast and using its power to explore other things, things I couldn't otherwise do. Mind-control, possession, speaking to Animals, changing my form; the possibility to do such things would be cool even after the horror of seeing what had become.<br /> <br /> <b>Dirge</b>: Deviant. My curiosity is not a strong wander drive. It grows in proportion to a thing's taboo nature. The only alternative would be 'Megalomaniac', as I am fascinated with the BIG and want to create an impact. It is not Idealistic or Visionary though as it is both fascinated with existing big things and it lacks the definite content of the other two, being a more vague 'will-to-power'.<br /> <br /> <b>Mask</b>: Jester, Rebel, Questioner, Scholar. My above curiosity is given a publicly acceptable face in the previous four. Plus, I see myself naturally filling those roles anyway. In the case of the Megalomaniac, maybe Idealist and Visionary can cover up the desire to make an impact for the sake of making an impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":". 12-31-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}